From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: denfry <dabinayo@pm.me>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 09:09:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Return the global tick from getCurrentTick on the global
 thread

Plugins in compatibility mode run their sync tasks on the global region
thread. Bukkit.getCurrentTick() only looked at the current region, so it
threw "No currently ticking region" there and a repeating task that reads
the tick failed every tick. The global tick has its own counter, use it.

diff --git a/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/RegionizedServer.java b/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/RegionizedServer.java
index 46751b44278961c5080bf3008f32e1471525b40e..036ec932f3624d25b7821cba79127161f3a8aa0a 100644
--- a/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/RegionizedServer.java
+++ b/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/RegionizedServer.java
@@ -141,6 +141,11 @@ public final class RegionizedServer {
             if (TickThread.isShutdownThread()) {
                 return 0L;
             }
+            // Tessera start - the global tick has its own tick count, compat plugin tasks run on it
+            if (isGlobalTickThread()) {
+                return INSTANCE.tickHandle.getCurrentTick();
+            }
+            // Tessera end - the global tick has its own tick count, compat plugin tasks run on it
             throw new IllegalStateException("No currently ticking region");
         }
         return region.getData().getCurrentTick();
